 *   "--verbose"   is the option "verbose" with the value "true"
 * Anything else is positional, and so is a single-dash argument like "-v".
 *
 * A lone "--" is a SEPARATOR: it is never itself an option or a positional,
 * and every argument AFTER it is positional even if it starts with "--".
 *
 * For args = {"build", "--verbose", "--out=dist", "main.java", "--",
 *             "--not-an-option", "-v"}:
 *   options(args)     -> {verbose=true, out=dist}      (size 2)
 *   positionals(args) -> [build, main.java, --not-an-option, -v]
